{
  "instruction": "Analyze the supplied sections as one teaching unit using only their Evidence. Keep learner-worthy Concepts and Claims even without edges. Group properties and repeated numeric variants as Claims; keep concrete instances, tasks or contrasting implementations as separate Concepts when needed for a useful relation. Do not make every slide, code line or output a Concept. Merge only identical meanings. Aliases are equivalent names, not members or examples. A heading cannot supply a missing procedure.\nSources are text Evidence rows [id,page,kind,exact_text], or labelled full-page PDF images. Image labels give the PDF page and integer Evidence ID. Use only the supplied source modality; images may supply facts, code, table structure and diagram relationships, but do not infer unseen content. A diagram arrow alone does not establish a learning prerequisite. Existing catalog: k=key,l=label,a=aliases,c=claims,e=evidence ids. Return only new/changed Concepts and new Relations; reuse a key only for the same meaning. Claims cite only supplied text or image Evidence IDs. IDs are document-global first-column values, never page numbers or renumbered positions.\nOutput Concept: {k:short unique key,l:label,a:[aliases],c:[Claims]}. Claim: {m:concise grounded meaning,s:[evidence ids]}. Select complete Evidence units; include required continuations. Always set m to a concise, complete source-supported statement; do not use null. To explain a larger program, use concise grounded prose instead of repeating the program in each Claim; full source stays attached. Preserve necessary scope/conditions and the technical literals you state; unrelated source literals need not be repeated. Never emit character offsets or copied quotes.\nRelation: {s:source key,t:target key,k:type,r:specific short learner-facing reason,e:[endpoint Claim evidence ids],c:confidence 0..1}. Types and source -> target:\nprerequisite: necessary knowledge -> dependent task/knowledge. Evidence must establish necessity, not helpful background or slide order.\npart_of: actual constituent -> whole, not a general subtype, chapter or declaration syntax.\napplication: concept/method -> concrete task/result accomplished with it, not a definition or representation.\nexample: abstract concept -> concrete instance, not automatically a general subtype.\ncontrast: the two entities themselves compared on an explicit axis, symmetric. Describing how they differ supplies an axis without using the word contrast. Queue FIFO versus stack LIFO is queue <-> stack, not comparison-topic <-> stack.\nRetain every precise grounded relation. Check source, target and direction against the reason; evidence about another method or endpoint does not support it. Cite only the union of both endpoints' Claim evidence IDs. Correct wrong types/endpoints when supported; otherwise omit. Never invent missing facts or procedures.\nUse natural Traditional Chinese, preserving technical names. Return strictly valid {concepts:[...],relations:[...]} JSON only. Escape each literal backslash in JSON; never turn a C escape into a raw or Unicode control character. Prefer words such as null character when no code literal is needed.",
